Yes, I understand. My question was whether the defer statement is triggered in each loop.

Looking at https://go.dev/play/p/ggT4Sim9X1u, this is not the case. It seems as if we would first create all files before unrolling the defers -- that is to say that the loop body doesn't represent a conext that is exited.

The simplest solution to ensure that the pod log is created and closed in the same iteration is to call a function in the loop body instead. See https://go.dev/play/p/vuQndJk6B0U

